#====================================================================
# E329 - Synchronize valid-abort tests with explicit termination
#====================================================================

id:                     E365
trigger_tool:           conan|mpiexec|hydra
phase:                  test
error_signature:        valid PMI abort control returned 1 for valid-int-(max|min)

severity:               2
category:               abort, mpi, openharmony, process-control, test-oracle
match_keywords:         MPICH, Hydra, PMI abort, disable-auto-cleanup, valid INT_MIN, valid INT_MAX, stale test oracle, delayed canary
title:                  Synchronize valid-abort tests with launcher termination semantics

root_cause:             After the production abort handler stopped treating disabled automatic cleanup as a successful return, the valid INT_MIN and INT_MAX probes still expected the launcher and ranks to survive, write canaries, finalize, and return zero. The stale oracle therefore rejected the required nonzero abort termination even though cleanup completed and no process residue remained.
affected_scope:         MPI launcher tests that change explicit abort behavior while retaining historical expectations derived from an automatic-cleanup option.
verification_cmd:       Run the valid-abort directed validator for two positive modes, four negatives, 26 single-fragment mutations, and C11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror; replay the complete ordered patch set forward and reverse with Git, GNU patch, and patch_ng.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           termination-bound-valid-abort-oracle
rec_description:        Accept the expected nonzero launcher result only through the managed cleanup path; bind the three live role/rank/PID/PGID records and exact proxy topology, reject PMI parser errors, require exact armed evidence, forbid a delayed survival canary, prove zero residue, and run a fresh ordinary MPI smoke case.
rec_command:            python validate_valid_abort_termination.py
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-package-managed-mpi

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      none
fallback_description:   Do not restore the production early-success return or weaken cleanup checks to preserve the old test result.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       valid PMI abort control returned.*raise|return HYD_SUCCESS.*auto_cleanup
forbid_1_reason:        Requiring return zero or restoring the early success path contradicts explicit abort termination.
forbid_1_consequence:   A real MPI_Abort can continue running when automatic cleanup is disabled.

forbid_2_pattern:       ignore_errors.*(?!require_launcher_cleanup)|canary.*required
forbid_2_reason:        Ignoring the nonzero result without cleanup and topology binding can accept a crash, parser rejection, or leaked launcher.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test can pass without proving that the intended abort path terminated the complete job.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

